# Bitcoin Agent Exchange - API configuration template
# Copy this file to .env in the repository root, then fill in only what you use:
#   cp .env.example .env
# Never put real credentials in this example or commit your local .env.
# Offline demos/tests do not require API keys. You do not need every provider.
#
# Loading:
# - The dashboard reads Gemini keys from the project-root .env.
# - Live collectors read CoinGecko and SoSoValue keys from the project .env.
# - experiments.live_attack and experiments.news_robustness load .env
#   (or the path supplied with --env-file); existing environment values win.
# - Other model-client entry points may require exporting these variables or
#   explicitly calling dotenv.load_dotenv() before constructing the client.
# - Restart the dashboard after changing its environment.
# - Setting a key alone does not start forecasts, trades, or scheduled jobs.

# --- Gemini: dashboard News/Mood, debate, and Gemini experiments ---
# Set GOOGLE_API_KEY; GEMINI_API_KEY is an alternative for the demo/dashboard.
# The general Google model client uses GOOGLE_API_KEY.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional model override for the demo/dashboard/experiment Gemini client.
# Omit to use the code default; choose a model available to your account.
# GEMINI_MODEL=

# --- Market data ---
# CoinGecko demo key: live stablecoin collection.
COINGECKO_DEMO_API_KEY=
# SoSoValue key: automatic refresh of US spot Bitcoin ETF net flows.
# Sent as x-soso-api-key to openapi.sosovalue.com.
# Without a key, the dashboard uses the saved data/etf_flows.csv.
SOSOVALUE_API_KEY=

# --- Cross-provider experiments: python -m experiments.live_attack ---
# --provider claude uses ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; --provider openai uses OPENAI_API_KEY.
# These do not switch the dashboard's model provider.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Optional demo-provider model overrides; omit to use code defaults.
# CLAUDE_MODEL=
# OPENAI_MODEL=

# --- Optional general model-client providers ---
# Only needed when explicitly selecting the corresponding provider through
# model_clients.factory. Pass provider and model names to create_llm_client().
# These clients may need additional optional SDK packages.
# XAI_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=
# DASHSCOPE_CN_API_KEY=
# ZHIPU_API_KEY=
# ZHIPU_CN_API_KEY=
# MINIMAX_API_KEY=
# MINIMAX_CN_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=
# International and China-region provider keys are not interchangeable.

# --- Optional Azure OpenAI client ---
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=
# AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT_NAME=
# OPENAI_API_VERSION=

# --- Optional Amazon Bedrock client ---
# Use ONE authentication method: Bedrock bearer token OR the AWS credential
# chain (an existing AWS profile, environment credentials, or an IAM role).
# AWS_REGION=
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=
# AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=
# AWS_PROFILE=
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=

# --- Optional local / generic OpenAI-compatible clients ---
# Ollama needs no API key. Its default endpoint is http://localhost:11434/v1.
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# For a keyed generic endpoint; leave unset for a keyless local server.
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_API_KEY=
# Pass a generic endpoint's base_url explicitly to create_llm_client(...).

# Public data paths currently need no project API credentials for Binance
# market data, Coin Metrics community data, Yahoo, Alternative.me, DefiLlama,
# Coinbase, and the public Kalshi/Limitless observation tools.
# No n8n integration or n8n credentials are configured by this project.
